---
// Multiverse exploration (#418 (technique pages, part 2)): the tree of an
// exploration of the register with the planted bug. The explorer forks, so
// the tree is recorded natively (crates/moonpool-wasm-demo/tests/
// exploration_tree.rs, src/runs/exploration.json); public/exploration.js
// draws it.
import { Code } from "astro:components";
import Technique from "../../../layouts/Technique.astro";
import { url } from "../../../nav";
import { excerpt, repoFile } from "../../../lib/source.mjs";
import tree from "../../../runs/exploration.json";

const test = repoFile("crates/moonpool-wasm-demo/tests/exploration_tree.rs");
const config = excerpt(test, "fn exploration() -> ExplorationConfig {", "max_recipe_len: 6,", 2);
const explore = excerpt(test, "fn explore(seed: u64) -> SimulationReport {", ".expect(\"the site's config is valid\")", 1);
const bugIndex = tree.nodes.findIndex((n) => n.failed);
const bug = tree.nodes[bugIndex];
---
<Technique
  title="Multiverse exploration"
  description="At each new discovery, the run forks. The children try other futures from the same moment."
  guide={[
    "part5-building-on-top/01-exploration.md",
    "part5-building-on-top/02-exploration-problem.md",
    "part5-building-on-top/03-frontier-controller.md",
    "part5-building-on-top/05-exemplars-continuations.md",
    "part5-building-on-top/06-multi-seed.md",
  ]}
>
  <h2>The problem</h2>
  <p>A bug can need two rare things, one after the other. Each new seed starts from zero, so it must find the
    first rare thing again before it can try for the second. The chance is the product of the two, and most
    seeds never get near.</p>

  <h2>The technique</h2>
  <p>A run is a stream of random numbers. A <b>recipe</b> is a list of <code>(draw count, seed)</code> pairs:
    replay the stream up to that draw, then go on with a new seed. When a run makes a discovery that no run
    made before (a coverage assertion fires for the first time, a bucket fills, a watermark rises), the
    explorer forks it there: the children replay the run up to the discovery, then each takes another
    future. A productive child forks again; a child with nothing new ends its branch. A failing child is a
    bug, with the recipe that replays it.</p>
  <p><code>moonpool-explorer</code> forks processes and shares memory between them, so it does not run in a
    browser. A Rust test ran this exploration and recorded its tree.</p>

  <h2>The live run</h2>
  <p>Seed {tree.seed} of the register with the planted bug. Its root timeline passes. The explorer ran {tree.nodes.length} timelines:
    each column is one, in the order it ran, and each row is a depth. Step through them, or select one.
    Timeline {bugIndex} forks from timeline {bug.parent} at draw {bug.fork_at} and breaks the invariant. The engine replays it from its recipe in your browser.</p>
  <div class="breakout">
    <div class="run">
      <div class="run-head label"><span>the timelines of seed {tree.seed}</span><span>+ discovery · ✗ bug · ○ nothing new</span></div>
      <div class="tree-wrap"><svg id="tree-svg" class="tree" role="img" aria-label="The tree of the exploration"></svg></div>
      <div class="switches">
        <button class="btn small" type="button" id="tree-step">Next timeline</button>
        <button class="btn small" type="button" id="tree-all">All</button>
        <button class="btn small" type="button" id="tree-bug">The bug</button>
        <button class="btn small" type="button" id="tree-root">The root</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tree-info" id="tree-info" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </div>
    <section class="run run-under" id="run" aria-label="A timeline in the player"></section>
    <noscript><p>The live run needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  </div>
  <script is:inline type="application/json" id="tree" set:html={JSON.stringify(tree).replace(/</g, "\\u003c")} />

  <h2>The code</h2>
  <p>The settings of this exploration. <code>workers: 0</code> runs each timeline in the process, one after
    the other, so the tree is the same each time:</p>
  <Code theme="css-variables" lang="rust" code={config} />
  <p>The test turns it on, and keeps the tree in the report:</p>
  <Code theme="css-variables" lang="rust" code={explore} />
  <p>The report gives each bug as a <code>BugRecipe</code>. <code>replay_timeline(seed, recipe)</code> runs
    that one timeline again.</p>
  <script is:inline type="module" src={url("exploration.js")}></script>
</Technique>
